/div><div class="_Y3Itb_media-popover-review-container_1dLQH"><div class="a-section _Y3Itb_cr-media-popover-sidepanel-container_1EUvC"><div class="a-section a-spacing-small _Y3Itb_cr-media-popover-sidepanel-header-section_3TxI7 _Y3Itb_cr-media-popover-sidepanel-header-section-truncated_DITiq"><div data-reviewbind="ProfileBlock"><a href="javascript:void(0)" class="a-profile" data-a-size="small"><div aria-hidden="true" class="a-profile-avatar-wrapper"><div class="a-profile-avatar"><img src="https://images-na.ssl-images-amazon.com/images/G/01/x-locale/common/grey-pixel.gif" class="a-lazy-loaded"/><noscript><img/></noscript></div></div><div class="a-profile-content"><span class="a-profile-name">Amazon Customer</span></div></a></div><div class="_Y3Itb_rating-and-profile-badges-container_348ae"><i data-reviewbind="Rating" class="a-icon a-icon-star-small a-star-small-5 a-spacing-top-micro _Y3Itb_rating-block_2mVHa"><span class="a-icon-alt">5 out of 5 stars</span></i><div class="aok-hidden" data-reviewbind="RatingAlt" data-multiple-starts-suffix="Stars" data-one-star-suffix="Star"></div><div data-reviewbind="ProfileBadge" class="_Y3Itb_profile-badges-container_k5lqb"></div></div><h5 lang="en-CA" data-reviewbind="ReviewTitle" class="_Y3Itb_cr-sidepanel-title_EX93d _Y3Itb_cr-sidepanel-truncated-title_2w0Qj">It’s great, love the customization</h5><div lang="en-CA" class="_Y3Itb_cr-sidepanel-text-with-gradient_3T4-j"><div data-reviewbind="ReviewText" class="_Y3Itb_cr-sidepanel-text_3MYCz _Y3Itb_cr-sidepanel-truncated-text_3nfmo">Review is for Razer Naga V2 Hyperspeed, not V2 Pro. I don’t understand most of the other reviews. If the software sucks, just assign the keys once and don’t use it until you need to re-assign the keys. To the guy that said one scroll forward, two scrolls back, maybe don’t use hyperscroll if you’re not comfortable?? lol Took me a week to get used to this mouse(I have only used regular mice before this), and about 2 more weeks to build muscle memory for using 12 buttons. The mouse is great, I have no complaints. Buy from Amazon (not a third party seller) instead of Razer website, so you don’t have to deal with Razer’s crappy customer support. I also see mentions of issues with unintentional clicking, don’t buy sensitive mice if your hands are not used to them, or learn to rest your hand on the mouse instead of squeezing it. When you plug the mouse into a computer, it will automatically download the software. After the installation is complete, you might want to disable it at startup from the task manager. You might have to look up how to assign keys if you’re doing it for the first time, but after you’ve done it once it’s easy. You can set up multiple profiles for different games/softwares, but you will have to switch them using the Razer software. I have been using this mouse for about a month and have not experienced any issues. I will update this review if I do.</div><div class="_Y3Itb_cr-sidepanel-container-gradient_1zm2j _Y3Itb_cr-sidepanel-container-gradient-truncated_3zXR9"></div></div><div class="_Y3Itb_cr-sidepanel-text-expansion-section_2guev"><a data-mix-operations="expandTextClickHandler" data-mediatype="IMAGE" href="javascript:void(0)" aria-expanded="false" class="_Y3Itb_cr-sidepanel-expander-see-more_1sipE" role="button"><span class="_Y3Itb_cr-sidepanel-expander-icon_1dF4M"><i class="a-icon a-icon-expand a-icon-mini" role="presentation"></i></span><span class="_Y3Itb_cr-sidepanel-expander-text_oEWO4"><span>More</span></span></a><a data-mix-operations="hideTextClickHandler" data-mediatype="IMAGE" href="javascript:void(0)" aria-expanded="true" class="_Y3Itb_cr-sidepanel-expander-see-less_1Hpji" role="button"><span class="_Y3Itb_cr-sidepanel-expander-icon_1dF4M"><i class="a-icon a-icon-collapse a-icon-mini" role="presentation"></i></span><span class="_Y3Itb_cr-sidepanel-expander-text_oEWO4"><span>Hide</span></span></a></div><ul class="_Y3Itb_media-popover-thumbnail-image-container_1q_4Q" data-imagealttext