lapsed a-hidden">Brief content visible, double tap to read full content.</div><div class="a-teaser-describedby-expanded a-hidden">Full content visible, double tap to read brief content.</div><div data-csa-c-slot-id="customer_review-R236BI0JTMUCDG_6_review_text" data-csa-c-type="element" class="a-cardui _Y3Itd_peek-expand_3G9Ub" data-a-card-type="peekExpand"><div class="a-cardui-body _Y3Itd_no-padding_1A9ha"><div class="a-reactive-container"><div><div class="a-cardui-content a-cardui-uninitialized" data-a-max-height="300" style="max-height:300px"><div class="_Y3Itd_relative_1SChh"><div data-hook="reviewRichContentContainer" lang="en-CA" class="_Y3Itd_contain-rich-content_2IORW"><p><span>The shelf looks nice after it&#x27;s mounted but getting it to that point was a struggle. The instructions to assemble the shelf are good but you&#x27;re basically on your own to mount it.  The mounting holes do no line up with your standard stud spacing so it will require anchors to fasten it properly. It comes with some crappy drywall anchors and no instructions. I highly recommend purchasing a 4 pack of &quot;snap toggle&quot; anchors from home depot before you attempt to mount this.</span></p></div></div></div></div><div class="a-reactive-container-gradient"></div></div></div><div data-hook="reviewExpandButtonContainer" class="a-cardui-footer _Y3Itd_no-padding_1A9ha"><div class="a-cardui-expand-control-footer _Y3Itd_read-more-less_2uDYd" data-csa-c-type="widget" data-csa-interaction-events="click"><a href="javascript:void(0)" class="a-cardui-expand-control-footer-button" role="button"><span class="a-expander-icon"><i class="a-css-icon"></i></span><span class="a-see-more a-color-link"><span class="a-see-more-text" style="display:none">Read more</span><span class="a-see-less-text" style="display:none">Read less</span></span></a></div></div></div></div><div data-hook="translationSpinner" class="_Y3Itd_single-review-translation-spinner-container_ypxf2"><div class="a-spinner-wrapper _Y